WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.570
Let’s talk about your gut, and changes in your bowels.

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:10.420
The gut card describes pain, bloating, and changes in bowel habits.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:17.560
Inflammatory bowel disease, or IBD, can happen in some people with PsA.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:21.700
IBD means inflammation of the digestive tract.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:29.130
But a bowel change does not prove that you have IBD, or that PsA is the cause.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:34.300
Tell your care team about gut symptoms that keep happening.

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:39.020
Note what changed, when it started, and how it affects your day.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:45.130
Your team may ask about your medicines, and decide whether you need more tests.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:51.840
If symptoms are severe, or you feel very unwell, get urgent medical help.

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:55.910
Great job! Let’s review.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:01.850
A bowel change does not prove that you have IBD or that PsA is the cause.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.820
Tell your care team about gut symptoms that keep happening.
